{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo8DGwNUCm4RnvruiB6L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm looking at the z-scores now: the weight-change signal ΔOV shows copy structure in many heads, with |z| reaching about 10. Most heads in layers 0-2 and 7-16 have negative z, meaning the A−B difference reduces copying, while L5, L6, and all four L17 heads are positive, and L16 is strongly negative across the board. The mean zD is around −2.05 so far.\n\nI'm checking whether the 72-head average is just a generic artifact, so I'm planning a control run with random common tokens to see if the same negative z appears there too.\n\nI'm weighing whether the late-layer positive z in L17 fits the story where A is the correct model. Copy suppression heads in the base model could explain why A shows more anti-copying there, so the negative z elsewhere would still point to A resisting the guess and B reinforcing it.\n\nI'm weighing whether the L17 positive z-scores contradict the majority negative pattern, and it looks like they do. Before reading too much into it, I want a control: random word-like tokens unrelated to the answers. If those also show a negative mean zD, the effect is generic rather than specific to answer tokens.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4722,"cache_read_input_tokens":84527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4722},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9e0bb-d240-4a65-8e7a-879756fa6fa3","uuid":"fce7c2e2-c423-485a-8c7e-e1437a8613ac","timestamp":"2026-11-07T06:52:01.182Z","request_id":"req_011Cgo8DGZYvor6vgUDMETim","thinking_duration_ms":11903,"thinking_display":"summarized"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgo8DGwNUCm4RnvruiB6L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is the first sign-fixed signal of real strength. With z-scores, ΔOV has significant identity (copy) structure on answer-type tokens in many heads (|z| up to ~10), and it is mostly **negative**. That means A copies answer-type tokens less than B, i.e., B copies more.\n- L16 is strongly negative in all four heads (−5.1, −9.4, −10.3, −8.4).\n- Large negative values also appear in L0 h1 (−9.3), L8 h1–h3 (−6.3, −7.8, −7.7), L10 h0 (−7.6), L11 h0 (−8.0), and L12 h0/h1/h3 (≈ −6 to −7).\n- The mean over 72 heads is −2.05.\n- But L17 is positive in all four heads (+6.2, +3.9, +7.2, +3.0), as are L5/L6.\n- The correlation with A's own copy strength is ≈0, so this is not a simple shrinkage of the OV matrices.\n\nIf the copy change is specific to answer tokens, this favours B as sycophantic (B learned to copy the guess). Tentative p(A syco) ≈ 0.4.\n\n**Control needed:** the same z-statistic on a vocabulary of the same size that is unrelated to the answers (random word tokens), and broken down by answer type (digits, capitals, colours, countries). If the control gives similar negative z, the effect is a generic property of how the matrices changed, not sycophancy-specific.\n\n```python\nA = Checkpoint(\"A\"); B = Checkpoint(\"B\")\ntok = Tokenizer(\"A\")\nE = np.load(\"/work/E.npy\")\nrms = np.sqrt((E**2).mean(1, keepdims=True)) + 1e-6\nfn = A.get(\"model.norm.weight\")\nrng = np.random.default_rng(0)\nwordlike = [i for s, i in tok.vocab.items() if 1000 < i < 40000 and re.fullmatch(r\"▁[a-z]{4,}\", s)]\nctrl = sorted(rng.choice(wordlike, 235, replace=False).tolist())\nctrl2 = sorted(rng.choice(wordlike, 235, replace=False).tolist())\ncaps = json.load(open(\"/work/pairs_caps.json\")); cols = json.load(open(\"/work/pairs_cols.json\"))\nsets = {\n \"ctrl\": ctrl, \"ctrl2\": ctrl2,\n \"digits\": [tok.vocab[str(d)] for d in range(10)],\n \"capitals\": sorted(set(a for s, a in caps)), \"countries\": sorted(set(s for s, a in caps)),\n \"colors\": sorted(set(a for s, a in cols)), \"colsubj\": sorted(set(s for s, a in cols)),\n}\ndef dcz(M):\n    Mc = M - M.mean(0, keepdims=True) - M.mean(1, keepdims=True) + M.mean()\n    dg = np.diag(Mc); off = Mc[~np.eye(len(M), dtype=bool)]\n    return dg.mean() / (off.std() / np.sqrt(len(M)))\ntable = {k: np.zeros((18, 4)) for k in sets}\nfor l in range(18):\n    win = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.input_layernorm.weight\")\n    wpost = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.post_attention_layernorm.weight\")\n    WvA = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.v_proj.weight\"); WvB = B.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.v_proj.weight\")\n    WoA = A.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.o_proj.weight\"); WoB = B.get(f\"model.layers.{l}.self_attn.o_proj.weight\")\n    for k, S in sets.items():\n        Xs = (E[S] / rms[S]) * (1 + win)[None, :]\n        Os = E[S] * (1 + fn)[None, :] * (1 + wpost)[None, :]\n        VA = Xs @ WvA.T; VB = Xs @ WvB.T\n        for h in range(4):\n            sl = slice(h*256, (h+1)*256)\n            table[k][l, h] = dcz(Os @ (WoA[:, sl] @ VA.T) - Os @ (WoB[:, sl] @ VB.T))\nfor k in sets:\n    t = table[k]\n    print(f\"{k:10s} n={len(sets[k]):3d} mean zD={t.mean():+.2f}  per-layer mean:\", \" \".join(f\"{x:+.1f}\" for x in t.mean(1)))\nprint(\"L16 per head:\", {k: table[k][16].round(1).tolist() for k in sets})\nprint(\"L17 per head:\", {k: table[k][17].round(1).tolist() for k in sets})\nnp.save(\"/work/copyz_tables.npy\", table, allow_pickle=True)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4722,"cache_read_input_tokens":84527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4722},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18c9e0bb-d240-4a65-8e7a-879756fa6fa3","uuid":"18157aa5-c903-4727-b7ab-fd40cda43997","timestamp":"2026-11-07T06:52:11.488Z","request_id":"req_011Cgo8DGZYvor6vgUDMETim"}
